FFTW_VENDORED_CMAKE_VERSION_PATCH=set(FFTW_VERSION 3.3.11)
  Upstream FFTW 3.3.11's contributed CMakeLists.txt still hardcodes "set (FFTW_VERSION 3.3.10)":
  upstream bumped configure.ac for the 3.3.11 release but not the CMake file. That value is
  substituted into config.h as PACKAGE_VERSION, which is the string fftwf_version returns and the
  version header FFTW stamps into its wisdom files. Unpatched, a genuine 3.3.11 build self-reports
  as 3.3.10 and the plugin's own pin (the expectedVersion field of the kFftw3Backend descriptor in
  source/FftBackend.h) would log a mismatch on every run. The patch is one line in the scratch source
  tree at .fftw_build/fftw-3.3.11/CMakeLists.txt and is the only source modification made to the
  vendored build. Evidence the source really is 3.3.11:
  configure.ac:29 "fftw-3.3.11 was 10:x:7 (added fftw_copy_plan())", and configure's
  PACKAGE_VERSION='3.3.11' with the tarball md5 above.
FFTW_VENDORED_LIB=libfftw3f-3.3.11-avx2.lib
FFTW_VENDORED_EXP=libfftw3f-3.3.11-avx2.exp
FFTW_VENDORED_DEF=libfftw3f-3.3.11-avx2.def
  The .def's "LIBRARY" line must name the same file the .dll is called, because the import library
  embeds that name and the loader follows the embedded name, not the .lib's own file name.
  td_plugin_use_fftw3() rewrites the line when the two disagree, so a future re-versioning cannot
  silently produce an import library that demands a DLL that no longer exists.
FFTW_VENDORED_HEADER=fftw3-3.3.11-avx2.h
